okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: 로컬에서 deepseek나 musespark를 사용할때 에러 (Codex TUI through the Ciel Router in G:\\ciel-bridge-service; muse-spark turn died with `input[0] did not match any supported type`, deepseek turns showed shell `exec` calls 'aborted', browser/computer 'unsupported call', and the turn ended with the thinking passthrough rejection)."
symptom:
  muse_spark: "2026-09-18T20:53:05 (01:53:05Z) thread 01a08e99 turn 01a0b75d: `event: error data: {\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\",\"message\":\"invalid_request_error: `input[0]` did not match any supported type\"}}`, turn duration 523 ms (rollout task_complete record)."
  deepseek: "same thread after relaunch with deepseek-v4-flash: exec calls answered `aborted`, sleep/js answered `unsupported call: <name>`, and the last turn ended at 20:58:13 with `invalid_request_error: The `content[].thinking` in the thinking mode must be passed back to the API` (router.log upstream_direct_http_error, code=400)."
isolation:
  cause: "The unit group's headless-update test performs a native launch and the runner isolates only part of the CLI state. On 2026-09-18 14:33 that sweep removed every Ciel slash command from the user's real ~/.claude/commands (ImportSession.md included). The commands were restored with install_ciel_runtime_slash_commands() + install_ciel_runtime_codex_prompts(), and runtime_paths.py now binds CLI_ASSET_HOME to the isolated config dir (CLAUDE_COMMANDS_DIR, CLAUDE_SETTINGS_PATH, CLAUDE_GATEWAY_CACHE, codex prompts, statusline script). Journal: fixes/runtime/cli-assets-wiped-by-test-sweep.okf."
shared_client_facts:
  client: "Codex CLI 0.155.1 (bin dir updated 2026-09-18 14:48), launched by the launcher as `codex.exe --yolo -c model_provider=ciel-runtime -c model_providers.ciel-runtime.base_url=http://127.0.0.1:9465/v1 -c wire_api=responses -c model_catalog_json=<meta catalog> -m <model> resume 01a08e99-...` (codex-processes/98964-client.json)."
  catalogue: "The model catalog entry the launcher writes sets `use_responses_lite: true` and `tool_mode: code_mode_only`, so the client carries its whole tool catalogue in an `additional_tools` input item ({type, role: developer, tools: [{type: namespace, name: functions|clock|collaboration|mcp__*, tools: [...]}]}) and leaves top-level tools empty. Captured from the real TUI (ConPTY) and from `codex app-server` with the same catalog: identical shapes."
deepseek_root_cause:
  rule: "DeepSeek's Anthropic-compatible endpoint refuses a thinking-mode request whose history holds ANY assistant message without a `thinking` block. Verified against the live API with the failing body: baseline 400; dropping the 3 thinking-less assistant messages 200; adding a synthesized thinking block (arbitrary signature) 200; `thinking: {type: disabled}` 200; requests truncated to the last 20/8 messages still 400 (the offender sits in the tail)."
  source_of_thinking_less_turns: "Two: (a) replayed cross-provider assistant turns (muse-spark/other models) that never had thinking; (b) turns the router itself retried with thinking disabled - live `codex_reasoning_budget_recovery provider=deepseek ... strategy=disable` at 20:55:28 produced an assistant turn without thinking, the client persisted it, and the following thinking-mode request was rejected."
  fix: "providers/deepseek.py: `_with_thinking_passthrough()` gives every assistant message that lacks a `thinking` block a placeholder block (THINKING_PASSTHROUGH_PLACEHOLDER + signature = uuid5 of a content digest, so the replayed prefix stays byte-stable for provider-side caching); applied in normalize_request_options whenever thinking is not explicitly disabled."
  verification: "Replayed the failing resumed thread (a copy of the 275 MB rollout) through an isolated router against the real DeepSeek API. Before: 4 upstream attempts, every one 400 `content[].thinking`. After: 11 upstream requests, no upstream error, 0 assistant messages without thinking, 2 synthesized placeholders in the first body. tests/test_deepseek_provider.py +3 (restore, cache-stable signature, disabled-mode untouched); router group 1138 OK; ruff clean."
muse_spark_status: "OPEN - not reproduced. The failing body is not recoverable: the Responses passthrough logs no upstream line at INFO, the router was not started with CIEL_RUNTIME_DUMP_UPSTREAM, and no TRACE level records request bodies. Every reconstruction tried with the current build answers 200 against Meta: (a) the TUI-shaped request carrying additional_tools at input[0] through an isolated router (hoist drops the item, model answers), (b) the same resumed thread via `thread/resume` with the muse-spark catalog (router compacts to 267 items, Meta answers), (c) the classic exec body from `codex exec`. Verified directly against Meta: `input` as a list with a string or an empty object at [0] answers `input[0] did not match any supported type` (so the failing body had a string/empty-object/unknown-type item at input[0]); a plain-string `input` answers 200."
next_capture: "Reproduce the muse-spark failure once with capture enabled: launch the TUI (or resume the thread) against an isolated router started with CIEL_RUNTIME_DUMP_UPSTREAM, or restart the workspace router with that variable set, then read the dumped body. That body decides between the open hypotheses (unhoistable/empty additional_tools catalogue left in place, an unknown item type, or a string element at input[0])."
tool_symptom_evidence:
  measured: "Response projection for the captured lite catalogue is correct in the current build: `functions__exec` (the alias the translated routes send upstream) projects to `custom_tool_call name=exec namespace=functions` with raw input, and `clock__sleep` to `function_call name=sleep namespace=clock`. Bare upstream names (exec, sleep) project without namespace, which is what the client answers with `unsupported call`."
  live: "The live deepseek turn's client-facing calls were recorded in the rollout as bare `function_call exec|js|sleep|wait` - i.e. that request's tool declaration did not reach the model as namespaced aliases, and `js`/`sleep` were never declared at all (the client answered `unsupported call`). The router log for those turns shows `POST /v1/responses ... tools=7` (converted count) while the first post-resume request logged `tools=0`."
  state: "Unresolved; needs the client request capture listed above (the incoming body is not logged on either route)."
state: "Working tree: providers/deepseek.py fix + 3 tests; committed separately from the muse capture work. Not deployed to the local snapshot."
